      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "BACKGROUND",
          "Label": "BACKGROUND",
          "content": "The aim of this study was to investigate the prevalence of obesity in Korean men with Klinefelter syndrome (KS) and the associated risk factors for obesity and hyperglycemia."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "METHODS",
          "content": "Data were collected retrospectively from medical records from 11 university hospitals in Korea between 1994 and 2014. Subjects aged ≥18 years with newly diagnosed KS were enrolled. The following parameters were recorded at baseline before treatment: chief complaint, height, weight, fasting glucose level, lipid panel, blood pressure, testosterone, luteinizing hormone, follicle-stimulating hormone, karyotyping patterns, and history of hypertension, diabetes, and dyslipidemia."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "Data were analyzed from 376 of 544 initially enrolled patients. The rate of the 47 XXY chromosomal pattern was 94.1%. The prevalence of obesity (body mass index ≥25 kg/m²) in Korean men with KS was 42.6%. The testosterone level was an independent risk factor for obesity and hyperglycemia."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSION",
          "content": "Obesity is common in Korean men with KS. Hypogonadism in patients with KS was associated with obesity and hyperglycemia."
        }
      ]},
